    <statement><p>The gas law for a fixed mass <m>m</m> of an ideal gas at absolute
temperature <m>T</m>, pressure <m>P</m>, and volume <m>V</m> is <m>PV = mRT</m>,
where <m>R</m> is the gas constant.</p>
<p>Find the partial derivatives</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial P}{\partial V} =</m><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial V}{\partial T} =</m><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial T}{\partial P} =</m><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial P}{\partial V} \frac{\partial V}{\partial T}\frac{\partial T}{\partial P} =</m><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/> (an integer)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-mRT}{V^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{mR}{P}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{V}{mR}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
